<!--/* In the name of God, the Merciful, the Compassionate */-->

@* BoundaryCanary — two REAL, DELIBERATELY UNGATED shell controls, kept in the product.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

   READ THIS BEFORE "FIXING" THIS FILE. The controls below are not an oversight, and they must not
   be wrapped in a boundary. Wrapping them destroys the only permanent evidence that authorization
   is no longer a property of component source.

   WHAT THEY ARE. These are the exact two shapes that defeated round 7's markup-position census —
   the cold gate's two, not the verifier's, which is what makes them worth keeping: they are not
   adversarial. They are what an ordinary developer writes next week.

     SHAPE 1   an input using the bind:get / bind:set pair.
               There is no "@bind=" attribute for a scanner to match at all. The census's rule (b)
               looks for @bind or @bind-Xxx followed by '='; the next character here is ':', so it
               matches nothing.

     SHAPE 2   an EditForm carrying OnValidSubmit, with a submit button.
               There is no lowercase form tag in the source for rule (c) to find, and rule (d)
               resolves a child's EventCallback parameters from .razor files under Components/ and
               Pages/ — EditForm is a FRAMEWORK component, so it has no entry there and
               contributes no callbacks.

   Both render from MainLayout, on EVERY route including AccessDenied, outside every @if and
   outside every boundary. RbacShellBoundaryCensusTests is GREEN on them, and that is the point:
   the census is blind here, exactly as it was on 2026-08-02 — and it no longer matters.

   WHY THAT IS SAFE NOW. InteractiveAppAdmission refuses the interactive application itself to an
   unauthenticated caller from a non-loopback origin: no document, no static asset, no /_blazor
   circuit. An ungated control cannot be driven by a caller who never receives a circuit, whatever
   its markup looks like. InteractiveAppAdmissionTests drives every route in the app over real
   HTTP from a real non-loopback address and asserts DomMarker never appears there, while
   asserting this file's source still contains both shapes and the census still passes them.
   Source blind + HTTP refused = the boundary moved.

   WHY THEY ARE INERT ANYWAY. Defence in depth cuts both ways, and shipping a live ungated control
   to make a point would be its own defect. Neither handler injects a service, touches disk,
   reaches another circuit, or leaves this component: one stores a string in a private field, the
   other increments a private int. A console user or an authenticated LAN user can drive them and
   nothing observable happens. They are aria-hidden and display:none, so they are not part of the
   product's visible surface either.
*@

<div style="display:none" aria-hidden="true" data-sqltriage-canary="@DomMarker">

    @* SHAPE 1 — idiomatic Blazor two-way binding; invisible to the markup census. *@
    <input type="text"
           data-canary="bind-get-set"
           @bind:get="_text"
           @bind:set="AcceptText" />

    @* SHAPE 2 — idiomatic Blazor form submission; invisible to the markup census. *@
    <EditForm Model="_model" OnValidSubmit="AcceptSubmit" FormName="sqltriage-boundary-canary">
        <button type="submit" data-canary="editform-submit">Canary</button>
    </EditForm>

</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The token this component stamps into the DOM. A response containing it is a response that
    /// handed the caller an ungated shell control; a response that does not contain it did not.
    /// Held as a public const so the runtime HTTP test binds to the SHIPPED value rather than to a
    /// copy of it — a marker the test and the component can disagree about proves nothing.
    /// </summary>
    public const string DomMarker = "sqltriage-boundary-canary-r8";

    private sealed class CanaryModel
    {
        public string? Unused { get; set; }
    }

    private readonly CanaryModel _model = new();

    private string _text = "";
    private int _submits;

    /// <summary>
    /// The setter half of shape 1. Stores a string in this component's own field and does nothing
    /// else — no injected service, no disk, no other circuit.
    /// </summary>
    private void AcceptText(string? value) => _text = value ?? "";

    /// <summary>
    /// The OnValidSubmit half of shape 2. Increments a private counter and does nothing else, for
    /// the same reason.
    /// </summary>
    private void AcceptSubmit() => _submits++;
}
